# Guitar (issues 107, redrawn): 1x1 tile at the south wall (col 1, row 6 of the main room). The body sits north-east with its dark sound hole and the neck runs south-west to the headstock and mist tuners, lit from the top-left; it rests on a small folding wooden stand (a V of two bars and a padded block, from Marc's photo) at the lower right. While the guitar is played the piece shows `guitar-stand` (the empty stand) instead.
size: 16x16
